<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  WEEPINGSTONES_RM_MOD_BUILD_1, Phase A (biome_mod_architecture.md §5) — the
  franchise-free RM_ copy of the campaign twin
  src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_WeepingStones.xml (BIOME_
  OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1, 2026-09-09 — full sheet design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/
  weeping_stones.md, FROZEN). Terrain/weather/disease blocks are verbatim
  copies of that def; only three things differ, all per the arch doc's own
  rule:

    1. workerClass — the twin's `VanillaBiomes.BiomeWorker_DesertOasis` (a
       donor type) becomes this mod's own `RM_BiomeWorker_WeepingStones`
       (Source/RM_BiomeWorker_WeepingStones.cs), same shape as the Greentide/
       FloodedCanyon precedents. `generatesNaturally` stays false below —
       this biome is placed by hand (Oasis landmark authoring per
       OASIS_LANDMARK_PLACEMENT_1), never natural worldgen, so the worker's
       GetScore is inert by construction; it exists only so the field
       resolves to a real, self-contained type.
    2. wildAnimals — the twin's 8 `mlie.starwarsanimalcollection` rows
       (Ollopom/Fanback/Dewback/Boma/Dactillion/Bantha/Eopie/Jamel) are
       OMITTED here per Q11 (SW_FAUNA_NEVER_IN_RM_TIER_1) and instead ride
       src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/WildAnimals_WeepingStones.xml as
       PatchOperationAdds casting their existing RSW_ ports. Only the two
       non-Star-Wars rows (ColossusToad, vanilla Odyssey; AA_Eyeling, Alpha
       Animals) stay inline.
    3. fishTypes/rareCatchesSetMaker — point at this mod's OWN duplicated
       RM_ fish items (Defs/ThingDefs_Items/RM_WeepingStonesFish_Items.xml,
       Defs/ThingSetMakerDefs/RM_RareOasisCatches.xml) rather than the
       twin's RUT_ ones, so this mod is self-contained and the frozen twin
       keeps resolving its own RUT_ items independently — duplicated, not
       moved, exactly because the twin still carries the live world and must
       not lose anything it currently references (arch §5 step 4).

  WEEPINGSTONES_RM_MOD_BUILD_1, wave 2 (2026-09-24) — the WEEPING_STONES_
  DESIGN_SITTING_1 ruled cast now has ThingDefs (RM_WeepingStonesNatives.xml,
  RM_Gorrask.xml, RM_WeepingStonesNativeFlora.xml, this mod's Defs/
  ThingDefs_Races and ThingDefs_Plants) and is wired below: 8 invented fauna
  (RM_Sillik/RM_Mirrik/RM_Ssurr/RM_Kirruk/RM_Tirbak/RM_Burrak/RM_Vhakk/
  RM_Vellak), the canyon-filling crab (RM_Gorrask, adapted from AA_SummitCrab
  per the NIGHTSIDE_ICE_DESIGN_SITTING_1 ruling — v1 ships as a real,
  legendary-rare single-tile creature; true multi-tile landform occupation
  is a follow-on mechanic, not built here), and the 10 invented flora rows
  including RM_Shadefern, which now REPLACES the donor `AB_GreenRockFern`
  per that sitting's ruling 3. RM_Dewgourd (the farmed crop) also carries a
  low wild commonality near the pool ring per the roster's own note
  ("wild rows rare at pool ring") in addition to being sowable.

  STOCKED_POOL_BUILD_1, wave 2 — six of the eight stocked-pool bestiary rows
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/weeping_stones_stocked_pool_2026-09-24.md
  §2) are wired below per the two-def law (§0/§2): a wildAnimals pawn entry
  (floor/pen presence) plus a fishTypes item entry (the catchable half,
  RM_StockedPoolCatchItems.xml). RM_Murrin is UNTOUCHED here — its species
  selection is owed to FISH_BY_BIOME_1's successor, per wave 1's own note.
  RM_Vhorrin carries zero ambient commonality by design (spec §2d: "the
  stocked line's set-piece... an enormous single harvest"; RM_Vhorrin ThingDef
  header: "NOT placed on any wildAnimals list") — it is a PoolStock
  mismanagement-state spawn (owed, STOCKED_POOL_BUILD_1 wave 3), never a
  roaming wild animal. Commonalities follow the spec's own pyramid (§2:
  "baseline and the two small biters are common... the escaper and the beasts
  are uncommon... the tyrant is one per pool at most") scaled against the
  existing ColossusToad/AA_Eyeling entries above.
-->
<Defs>

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RM_WeepingStones</defName>
    <generatesNaturally>false</generatesNaturally>
    <label>the Weeping Stones</label>
    <description>High pale stone standing in the path of the sea-wind. Most of this country is bright, dry, wind-scoured ridge and shoulder -- but every cold shaded face of it weeps: thin black streaks of wet running down white rock, moss crowding the seep lines, and here and there a true pool with a green ring around it and a crowd at the water. An oasis here is never merely found water; it is a working thing, part stone, part machine, part congregation of everything that drinks.</description>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.WeepingStones.RM_BiomeWorker_WeepingStones</workerClass>
    <lakeBeachTerrain>SoilRich</lakeBeachTerrain>
    <riverbankTerrain>SoilRich</riverbankTerrain>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>1.5</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.4</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.5</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1.5</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>World/Biomes/ZBiome_Oasis</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>90</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Malaria</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>50</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>50</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Sand</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.95</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>SoftSand</terrain>
        <min>0.95</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>70</Clear>
      <Fog>25</Fog>
      <DryThunderstorm>1</DryThunderstorm>
      <Sandstorm MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">6</Sandstorm>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <TorrentialRain>0</TorrentialRain>
      <Overcast MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0</Overcast>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <ColossusToad MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.4</ColossusToad>  <!-- colossus toad - medium-resident, keep; vanilla Odyssey animal -->
      <AA_Eyeling MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Eyeling>  <!-- ikee - omen, import; non-Star-Wars donor, stays RM tier per Q9 -->
      <!-- STOCKED_POOL_BUILD_1 wave 2 — the stocked-pool bestiary's floor/pen
           half (two-def law). RM_Murrin and RM_Vhorrin deliberately excluded,
           see the header comment above. -->
      <RM_Skarrin>0.6</RM_Skarrin>  <!-- skarrin - ring-breaker, common -->
      <RM_Karrek>0.6</RM_Karrek>  <!-- karrek - flenser swarm, common -->
      <RM_Vizhik>0.25</RM_Vizhik>  <!-- vizhik - the walker, uncommon -->
      <RM_Loomu>0.2</RM_Loomu>  <!-- loomu - the caller, uncommon -->
      <RM_Huldu>0.2</RM_Huldu>  <!-- huldu - the warm one, uncommon -->
      <RM_Ivvol>0.05</RM_Ivvol>  <!-- ivvol - the tally, rare -->
      <!-- WEEPINGSTONES_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 wave 2 — the 8 invented natives ruled
           at WEEPING_STONES_DESIGN_SITTING_1 (2026-09-24), plus the canyon-
           filling crab ruled at NIGHTSIDE_ICE_DESIGN_SITTING_1 the same day. -->
      <RM_Sillik>0.8</RM_Sillik>  <!-- sillik - the prey base, weep-face licker -->
      <RM_Mirrik>0.6</RM_Mirrik>  <!-- mirrik - dew-smoke swarm, flier -->
      <RM_Ssurr>0.35</RM_Ssurr>  <!-- ssurr - the fan-dancer, tamable -->
      <RM_Kirruk>0.2</RM_Kirruk>  <!-- kirruk - ridge-flier, comb-wing soarer -->
      <RM_Tirbak>0.15</RM_Tirbak>  <!-- tirbak - walking cistern, caravan colossus -->
      <RM_Burrak>0.12</RM_Burrak>  <!-- burrak - well-digger; elder = burradar, same def -->
      <RM_Vhakk>0.08</RM_Vhakk>  <!-- vhakk - the warden, margin apex predator -->
      <RM_Vellak>0.08</RM_Vellak>  <!-- vellak - RM pilgrim herd, sail-comb strider -->
      <RM_Gorrask>0.02</RM_Gorrask>  <!-- gorrask - canyon-filling crab, legendary-rare; v1 single-tile, landform-scale placement owed -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <Plant_Reeds>1.0</Plant_Reeds>  <!-- sarnreed -->
      <RM_Shadefern>0.4</RM_Shadefern>  <!-- shadefern - RULED replacement for the donor AB_GreenRockFern (WEEPING_STONES_DESIGN_SITTING_1 ruling 3) -->
      <RUT_Dewshrooms MayRequire="mandrake.rut.rotsporekit">0.4</RUT_Dewshrooms>  <!-- dewshrooms; shared with The Rot's kit, left inline pending the shared-plant decision -->
      <Plant_Ambrosia>0.12</Plant_Ambrosia>  <!-- ambrosia bush -->
      <!-- WEEPINGSTONES_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 wave 2 — the other 9 invented flora
           rows ruled at WEEPING_STONES_DESIGN_SITTING_1 (2026-09-24). -->
      <RM_Dewblade>1.0</RM_Dewblade>  <!-- dewblade - the baseline green -->
      <RM_Weepmat>0.7</RM_Weepmat>  <!-- weep-mat - shade/weep-line corduroy mat -->
      <RM_Verdimoss>0.6</RM_Verdimoss>  <!-- verdimoss - the relic-dresser -->
      <RM_Bladderquill>0.5</RM_Bladderquill>  <!-- bladderquill - the forage staple, bladder-fruit -->
      <RM_Dripfringe>0.3</RM_Dripfringe>  <!-- dripfringe - the overhang register -->
      <RM_Salvecomb>0.2</RM_Salvecomb>  <!-- salvecomb - the medicine plant -->
      <RM_Rockfinger>0.15</RM_Rockfinger>  <!-- rockfinger - the tree, RULED name (was Sailfin) -->
      <RM_Steamfrond>0.1</RM_Steamfrond>  <!-- steamfrond - the seep-oasis signature -->
      <RM_Dewgourd>0.02</RM_Dewgourd>  <!-- dewgourd - the farmed crop; wild rows rare at pool ring, sowable everywhere else -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>17</wildPlantRegrowDays>
    <maxFishPopulation>660</maxFishPopulation>
    <fishTypes MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
      <freshwater_Common>
        <RM_Ikkal>1.2</RM_Ikkal>
        <RM_Tarrik>1</RM_Tarrik>
        <RM_Duul>0.8</RM_Duul>
      </freshwater_Common>
      <freshwater_Uncommon>
        <RM_Ullo>1</RM_Ullo>
        <RM_Ozhu>0.8</RM_Ozhu>
        <RM_Vobbal>0.5</RM_Vobbal>
        <!-- STOCKED_POOL_BUILD_1 wave 2 — the stocked line's catch half
             (two-def law); a colonist fishing the pool edge with no husbandry
             job running can still occasionally pull one of these up
             (RM_StockedPoolCatchItems.xml header). RM_Murrin/RM_Vhorrin
             excluded, see the wildAnimals comment above for why. -->
        <RM_SkarrinCatch>0.4</RM_SkarrinCatch>
        <RM_KarrekCatch>0.4</RM_KarrekCatch>
        <RM_VizhikCatch>0.2</RM_VizhikCatch>
        <RM_LoomuCatch>0.15</RM_LoomuCatch>
        <RM_HulduCatch>0.15</RM_HulduCatch>
        <RM_IvvolCatch>0.05</RM_IvvolCatch>
      </freshwater_Uncommon>
      <rareCatchesSetMaker>RM_RareOasisCatches</rareCatchesSetMaker>
    </fishTypes>
    <!-- WATER_TRUCE_RETRIBUTION_1, carried over from the frozen twin: a
         guilty hit landing within `radius` cells of standing water turns
         nearby wildlife against the aggressor faction. -->
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_WaterTruceExtension">
        <radius>10</radius>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
